+/// Reference: `itype::use_methods`, a `std::map<std::string, use_function>` (`src/itype.h`), filled by `use_function_reader_map` (`src/item_factory.cpp:1907-1920`).
+/// Three rules are only visible here and nowhere else: the keys come back **sorted by name** rather than in the order the data writes them; two entries with the
+/// same name **collapse**, because `emplace` keeps the first; and `repair_item` objects are **renamed** to their `item_action_type` before they are registered
+/// (`1858-1865`), so a repairkit's action is called `repair_metal` and not `repair_item`.
