+/// Reference: `material_type::_vitamins` and its accessor (`src/material.h:163-166`). This exists because the derivation that gives a food its vitamins from its
+/// materials (`src/item_factory.cpp:762-776`) multiplies these numbers, and a recording of the comestibles alone cannot say whether a disagreement is in the
+/// derivation or in the material data underneath it.
+void dump_material_vitamins( const std::string &path )
+{
+    std::FILE *out = std::fopen( path.c_str(), "wb" );
