+/// Every item type's comestible slot, resolved.
+///
+/// Reference: `islot_comestible` (`src/itype.h:147-248`) and its loader (`src/item_factory.cpp:3405-3441`). Two things about it are invisible in the JSON and are the reason
+/// this is a recording rather than a re-read of the data:
+///
+/// * **the slot merges on inheritance.** `Item_factory::load_slot` (`src/item_factory.cpp:2859-2868`) reuses the parent's slot and then calls `deserialize` with
+///   `was_loaded`, so a child that states only `calories` keeps its parent's `quench`, `spoils_in` and the rest. That is the opposite of the container members, whose
+///   stated value clears the list first.
+/// * **`addiction_type` reads a value `addiction_potential` supplies.** The weighted reader's default is `default_addict_potential`, and that member is itself loaded
+///   two lines earlier (`:3432-3435`), so an addiction written without a weight takes the item's own potential - which a child may have inherited.
+void dump_comestibles( const std::string &path )
+{
+    std::FILE *out = std::fopen( path.c_str(), "wb" );
